1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,429
It's November first. You wake up,

2
00:00:02,329 --> 00:00:03,848
make coffee at home...

3
00:00:03,748 --> 00:00:05,590
and open a little notebook.

4
00:00:05,790 --> 00:00:08,085
On the first page you write three

5
00:00:07,985 --> 00:00:09,749
words. No-Spend November.

6
00:00:09,949 --> 00:00:11,711
Thirty days. No extras.

7
00:00:11,611 --> 00:00:14,025
Only the things you really need.

8
00:00:14,225 --> 00:00:15,739
And by December first...

9
00:00:15,639 --> 00:00:17,919
you'll have an extra four hundred and

10
00:00:17,819 --> 00:00:19,511
twenty dollars in the bank.

11
00:00:19,911 --> 00:00:23,092
Your friend Mia is having a very different morning.

12
00:00:23,292 --> 00:00:25,815
Three packages are waiting at her door.

13
00:00:25,715 --> 00:00:28,735
She doesn't even remember ordering two of them.

14
00:00:28,935 --> 00:00:30,592
A phone case. A candle.

15
00:00:30,492 --> 00:00:33,233
Something called a 'mini waffle maker.'

16
00:00:33,433 --> 00:00:36,033
And Black Friday hasn't even started yet.

17
00:00:36,433 --> 00:00:38,609
Here's the thing. Mia isn't bad with

18
00:00:38,509 --> 00:00:39,763
money. She's normal.

19
00:00:39,963 --> 00:00:42,160
In a 2022 Slickdeals survey,

20
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:45,532
Americans said they spent about three hundred

21
00:00:45,432 --> 00:00:48,603
fourteen dollars a month on impulse buys.

22
00:00:48,803 --> 00:00:52,397
That's three thousand seven hundred sixty-eight dollars a year.

23
00:00:52,597 --> 00:00:54,818
On things nobody planned to buy.

24
00:00:55,218 --> 00:00:57,158
And it never feels like a lot.

25
00:00:57,358 --> 00:00:58,980
It's the total that hurts.

26
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:01,153
So why a no-spend month?

27
00:01:01,353 --> 00:01:04,165
Because it's not about suffering for thirty days.

28
00:01:04,365 --> 00:01:06,315
It's a reset. You find out what

29
00:01:06,215 --> 00:01:08,881
you really need... and what was just habit.

30
00:01:09,081 --> 00:01:10,668
And you're not alone.

31
00:01:10,568 --> 00:01:13,854
A Credit Karma survey found forty-two percent

32
00:01:13,754 --> 00:01:17,961
of Americans were doing or considering a no-buy challenge.

33
00:01:18,361 --> 00:01:20,647
But most people fail by day five.

34
00:01:20,847 --> 00:01:23,679
They start with no plan. Just willpower.

35
00:01:23,879 --> 00:01:26,984
And willpower loses to a flash sale every time.

36
00:01:27,184 --> 00:01:29,578
So you're going to do it differently.

37
00:01:29,478 --> 00:01:30,384
Step by step.

38
00:01:30,784 --> 00:01:33,583
Step one. Write your rules before you start.

39
00:01:33,783 --> 00:01:35,437
On the left side of the page

40
00:01:35,337 --> 00:01:36,881
you write: what's allowed.

41
00:01:37,081 --> 00:01:39,458
Rent. Bills. Groceries from a list.

42
00:01:39,358 --> 00:01:42,125
Gas. Medicine. Gifts you already planned.

43
00:01:42,325 --> 00:01:44,428
That's not spending. That's living.

44
00:01:44,828 --> 00:01:46,833
On the right side: what's paused.

45
00:01:47,033 --> 00:01:49,591
Takeout. Coffee shops. New clothes.

46
00:01:49,491 --> 00:01:52,189
Online shopping. Gadgets. Home decor.

47
00:01:52,389 --> 00:01:54,923
Not forever. Just for thirty days.

48
00:01:55,123 --> 00:01:57,764
Clear rules mean no arguing with yourself

49
00:01:57,664 --> 00:01:58,756
at the checkout.

50
00:01:59,156 --> 00:02:00,548
And one more rule.

51
00:02:00,448 --> 00:02:01,265
A big one.

52
00:02:01,465 --> 00:02:03,769
If something breaks and you truly need

53
00:02:03,669 --> 00:02:04,986
it... you replace it.

54
00:02:05,186 --> 00:02:07,937
A no-spend month isn't about being stubborn.

55
00:02:08,137 --> 00:02:09,670
It's about being honest.

56
00:02:10,070 --> 00:02:11,469
Then you set the goal.

57
00:02:11,669 --> 00:02:13,537
Where does the saved money go?

58
00:02:13,737 --> 00:02:16,126
For you, it's your emergency fund.

59
00:02:16,026 --> 00:02:18,011
It's at six hundred dollars,

60
00:02:17,911 --> 00:02:20,165
and you want it at one thousand.

61
00:02:20,365 --> 00:02:22,144
Now this month has a reason.

62
00:02:22,544 --> 00:02:24,459
Step two. The spending audit.

63
00:02:24,660 --> 00:02:26,948
You open your banking app and look

64
00:02:26,848 --> 00:02:28,750
at last October. Every line.

65
00:02:28,950 --> 00:02:31,444
You grab a highlighter and mark anything

66
00:02:31,344 --> 00:02:32,581
that wasn't a need.

67
00:02:32,781 --> 00:02:34,262
It takes twenty minutes.

68
00:02:34,162 --> 00:02:35,758
And it's a little painful.

69
00:02:36,158 --> 00:02:38,544
Coffee shops: sixty-two dollars.

70
00:02:38,744 --> 00:02:41,278
Delivery apps: one hundred eighteen.

71
00:02:41,478 --> 00:02:44,575
Online orders you forgot about: ninety-four.

72
00:02:44,775 --> 00:02:47,439
Random stuff at the store: seventy-one.

73
00:02:47,839 --> 00:02:50,213
Three hundred forty-five dollars.

74
00:02:50,113 --> 00:02:51,109
In one month.

75
00:02:51,309 --> 00:02:52,959
And you couldn't name half of it.

76
00:02:53,159 --> 00:02:54,769
That's the moment it clicks.

77
00:02:54,969 --> 00:02:57,646
This money isn't gone because you're poor.

78
00:02:57,546 --> 00:02:59,364
It's gone because it's easy.

79
00:02:59,764 --> 00:03:01,639
Step three. Close the doors.

80
00:03:01,839 --> 00:03:04,519
Spending is easy because stores make it

81
00:03:04,419 --> 00:03:06,371
easy. So you make it harder.

82
00:03:06,571 --> 00:03:09,610
First, you unsubscribe from every store email.

83
00:03:09,810 --> 00:03:12,609
Thirty-one of them. It feels amazing.

84
00:03:13,009 --> 00:03:15,460
Next, you delete your saved card from

85
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:16,985
shopping sites and apps.

86
00:03:17,185 --> 00:03:19,750
Now every purchase means getting up,

87
00:03:19,650 --> 00:03:22,695
finding your wallet, typing sixteen digits.

88
00:03:22,895 --> 00:03:24,792
And a minute is often enough to

89
00:03:24,692 --> 00:03:25,777
change your mind.

90
00:03:26,177 --> 00:03:29,232
Then you turn off notifications from shopping apps.

91
00:03:29,432 --> 00:03:31,549
And you move them off your home

92
00:03:31,449 --> 00:03:32,980
screen. Into a folder.

93
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:34,086
On the last page.

94
00:03:34,286 --> 00:03:36,494
Out of sight... really is out of mind.

95
00:03:36,694 --> 00:03:38,921
Mia? She has eleven shopping apps on

96
00:03:38,821 --> 00:03:39,926
her first screen.

97
00:03:40,326 --> 00:03:42,027
Step four. The wish list.

98
00:03:42,227 --> 00:03:43,756
You will still want things.

99
00:03:43,656 --> 00:03:45,237
That's normal. You're human.

100
00:03:45,437 --> 00:03:47,526
So when you see something you want,

101
00:03:47,426 --> 00:03:48,492
you don't buy it.

102
00:03:48,392 --> 00:03:49,514
You write it down.

103
00:03:49,714 --> 00:03:51,176
Name. Price. Date.

104
00:03:51,576 --> 00:03:54,834
Day three: a wool jacket. Eighty-nine dollars.

105
00:03:55,034 --> 00:03:57,818
Day eight: wireless earbuds. Fifty-nine.

106
00:03:58,018 --> 00:04:02,763
Day twelve: a board game everybody's talking about. Forty-five.

107
00:04:02,963 --> 00:04:04,488
Your list gets longer.

108
00:04:04,388 --> 00:04:06,431
And something strange happens.

109
00:04:06,831 --> 00:04:08,283
By the end of the month,

110
00:04:08,183 --> 00:04:09,634
you read the list again.

111
00:04:09,834 --> 00:04:11,375
And most of the things...

112
00:04:11,275 --> 00:04:12,990
you don't even want anymore.

113
00:04:13,190 --> 00:04:15,174
The jacket? You already have two.

114
00:04:15,374 --> 00:04:17,823
The wanting faded. The money stayed.

115
00:04:18,223 --> 00:04:20,996
Step five. Food. Because this is where

116
00:04:20,896 --> 00:04:22,754
most no-spend months die.

117
00:04:22,954 --> 00:04:24,988
It's seven p.m. You're tired.

118
00:04:24,888 --> 00:04:27,389
And the delivery app is right there.

119
00:04:27,589 --> 00:04:30,125
So on Sunday, you plan five dinners.

120
00:04:30,325 --> 00:04:32,280
One grocery trip. One list.

121
00:04:32,180 --> 00:04:34,343
Nothing else goes in the cart.

122
00:04:34,743 --> 00:04:37,105
You cook double on Sunday and Wednesday.

123
00:04:37,305 --> 00:04:40,148
Chili. Pasta bake. A big pot of soup.

124
00:04:40,348 --> 00:04:42,880
Leftovers go in the freezer, labeled.

125
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:45,735
So 'nothing to eat' is never true again.

126
00:04:46,135 --> 00:04:47,667
And for the hard nights,

127
00:04:47,567 --> 00:04:49,875
you make a 'lazy list' on the fridge.

128
00:04:50,075 --> 00:04:53,465
Eggs on toast. Quesadillas. Frozen dumplings.

129
00:04:53,665 --> 00:04:55,932
Ten minutes, about two dollars a plate.

130
00:04:56,132 --> 00:04:58,234
Cheaper than delivery fees alone.

131
00:04:58,634 --> 00:05:01,593
Meanwhile, Mia orders dinner four times a week.

132
00:05:01,793 --> 00:05:03,774
Twenty-eight dollars a time,

133
00:05:03,674 --> 00:05:05,051
after fees and tip.

134
00:05:05,251 --> 00:05:07,685
That's over four hundred dollars a month.

135
00:05:07,885 --> 00:05:09,810
For food that arrives cold.

136
00:05:10,210 --> 00:05:12,135
Coffee? You buy a bag of good

137
00:05:12,035 --> 00:05:13,709
beans for twelve dollars.

138
00:05:13,909 --> 00:05:15,621
It makes about thirty cups.

139
00:05:15,821 --> 00:05:17,319
Forty cents a cup...

140
00:05:17,219 --> 00:05:18,998
instead of five dollars.

141
00:05:19,198 --> 00:05:21,700
And honestly? It tastes like a small

142
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:22,901
win every morning.

143
00:05:23,301 --> 00:05:24,744
Step six. Free fun.

144
00:05:24,644 --> 00:05:28,560
Because a no-spend month can't feel like a punishment.

145
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:30,428
So you make a list of free

146
00:05:30,328 --> 00:05:31,212
things to do.

147
00:05:31,412 --> 00:05:33,275
Long walks. The library.

148
00:05:33,175 --> 00:05:34,597
A free museum day.

149
00:05:34,497 --> 00:05:36,213
A movie night at home.

150
00:05:36,413 --> 00:05:39,064
Board games you already own. All free.

151
00:05:39,464 --> 00:05:42,081
The library becomes your favorite place.

152
00:05:42,281 --> 00:05:46,010
Books, movies, even audiobooks on your phone. All free.

153
00:05:46,210 --> 00:05:48,675
You read more in November than all summer.

154
00:05:48,875 --> 00:05:50,813
It doesn't feel like losing.

155
00:05:50,713 --> 00:05:52,256
It feels like finding.

156
00:05:52,656 --> 00:05:55,415
Friends invite you to a forty-dollar brunch.

157
00:05:55,615 --> 00:05:56,786
You don't say no.

158
00:05:56,686 --> 00:05:58,740
You say, 'Come to mine instead.

159
00:05:58,640 --> 00:06:00,000
I'll make pancakes.'

160
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:02,969
Six people. Eight dollars of ingredients.

161
00:06:03,169 --> 00:06:04,692
Best brunch of the year.

162
00:06:05,092 --> 00:06:07,830
Step seven. And this is the secret one.

163
00:06:08,030 --> 00:06:10,221
Every day you don't spend on extras...

164
00:06:10,121 --> 00:06:12,423
you move the money you would have spent.

165
00:06:12,623 --> 00:06:14,656
Just ten or fifteen dollars.

166
00:06:14,556 --> 00:06:16,175
Straight into savings.

167
00:06:16,575 --> 00:06:18,296
You also mark a big X on

168
00:06:18,196 --> 00:06:19,444
a paper calendar.

169
00:06:19,644 --> 00:06:21,799
One X for every no-spend day.

170
00:06:21,999 --> 00:06:23,746
By week two, the row of X's

171
00:06:23,646 --> 00:06:26,368
is so pretty... you don't want to break it.

172
00:06:26,568 --> 00:06:29,391
That's the trick. You're not fighting temptation.

173
00:06:29,291 --> 00:06:30,892
You're protecting a streak.

174
00:06:31,292 --> 00:06:33,044
Week two is the hardest.

175
00:06:33,244 --> 00:06:34,859
The excitement is gone.

176
00:06:34,759 --> 00:06:36,968
Payday arrives. Your brain says,

177
00:06:36,868 --> 00:06:38,418
'You deserve a treat.'

178
00:06:38,618 --> 00:06:40,315
And you do deserve a treat.

179
00:06:40,515 --> 00:06:42,188
So you take a long bath,

180
00:06:42,088 --> 00:06:44,285
call your mom, and watch a movie

181
00:06:44,185 --> 00:06:45,399
you already have.

182
00:06:45,799 --> 00:06:47,003
And if you slip?

183
00:06:46,903 --> 00:06:49,072
One coffee, one impulse snack?

184
00:06:49,272 --> 00:06:51,212
You don't quit. You write it down

185
00:06:51,112 --> 00:06:52,048
and keep going.

186
00:06:52,248 --> 00:06:55,673
A no-spend month with three slips still saves hundreds.

187
00:06:55,873 --> 00:06:57,278
Quitting saves nothing.

188
00:06:57,678 --> 00:06:59,828
Then... the last week of November.

189
00:07:00,028 --> 00:07:01,136
Black Friday.

190
00:07:01,336 --> 00:07:03,151
Every app, every TV ad,

191
00:07:03,051 --> 00:07:05,686
every email screams 'Last chance!'

192
00:07:05,886 --> 00:07:09,321
This year, Black Friday is November twenty-seventh.

193
00:07:09,721 --> 00:07:11,803
But you planned for this on day one.

194
00:07:12,003 --> 00:07:14,393
Black Friday is your one exception.

195
00:07:14,293 --> 00:07:15,309
With one rule.

196
00:07:15,509 --> 00:07:17,683
You can buy only what was already

197
00:07:17,583 --> 00:07:20,071
on your list. Before the sale started.

198
00:07:20,271 --> 00:07:22,019
You need new winter boots.

199
00:07:21,919 --> 00:07:23,857
So you check the price now...

200
00:07:23,757 --> 00:07:25,124
and again on Friday.

201
00:07:25,524 --> 00:07:27,773
The boots drop from one hundred twenty

202
00:07:27,673 --> 00:07:29,073
dollars to eighty-four.

203
00:07:29,273 --> 00:07:30,649
You buy them. Done.

204
00:07:30,549 --> 00:07:32,059
You close the laptop.

205
00:07:32,259 --> 00:07:35,493
No 'while I'm here.' No 'free shipping over fifty.'

206
00:07:35,693 --> 00:07:38,379
Thirty-six dollars saved. On purpose.

207
00:07:38,779 --> 00:07:40,598
Mia has a Black Friday too.

208
00:07:40,798 --> 00:07:42,337
She doesn't have a list.

209
00:07:42,237 --> 00:07:43,417
She has a feeling.

210
00:07:43,617 --> 00:07:45,445
A TV she didn't plan for.

211
00:07:45,345 --> 00:07:48,416
Three sweaters. A smart speaker 'because it

212
00:07:48,316 --> 00:07:50,006
was forty percent off.'

213
00:07:50,206 --> 00:07:52,916
Six hundred dollars. On a credit card.

214
00:07:53,316 --> 00:07:54,973
And here's why that matters.

215
00:07:55,173 --> 00:07:56,896
If she pays it off slowly,

216
00:07:56,796 --> 00:07:59,643
at a credit card rate over twenty percent...

217
00:07:59,843 --> 00:08:02,695
those 'deals' get more expensive every month.

218
00:08:02,895 --> 00:08:05,322
A discount on a credit card isn't

219
00:08:05,222 --> 00:08:06,591
always a discount.

220
00:08:06,991 --> 00:08:09,464
December first. You open your notebook.

221
00:08:09,364 --> 00:08:10,680
And you do the math.

222
00:08:10,880 --> 00:08:15,334
Last October, your extras cost three hundred forty-five dollars.

223
00:08:15,534 --> 00:08:17,913
This November, you spent fifty-one.

224
00:08:17,813 --> 00:08:20,583
A few slips, plus the boots on your list.

225
00:08:20,783 --> 00:08:22,431
And the daily transfers?

226
00:08:22,331 --> 00:08:23,205
They add up.

227
00:08:23,605 --> 00:08:25,959
Four hundred and twenty dollars.

228
00:08:25,859 --> 00:08:28,142
Moved into your emergency fund.

229
00:08:28,342 --> 00:08:30,811
Your six hundred dollars is now one

230
00:08:30,711 --> 00:08:32,165
thousand and twenty.

231
00:08:32,365 --> 00:08:34,556
Goal reached. One month early.

232
00:08:34,756 --> 00:08:36,589
Not because you earned more.

233
00:08:36,489 --> 00:08:37,764
Because you paused.

234
00:08:38,164 --> 00:08:41,974
Mia's November? Over one thousand dollars on extras.

235
00:08:42,174 --> 00:08:44,038
Most of it on her card.

236
00:08:44,238 --> 00:08:47,184
And she feels like the month just... disappeared.

237
00:08:47,384 --> 00:08:48,870
Same paycheck as you.

238
00:08:48,770 --> 00:08:50,850
Completely different December.

239
00:08:51,250 --> 00:08:53,163
But the best part isn't the money.

240
00:08:53,363 --> 00:08:55,910
You found out you don't miss delivery.

241
00:08:55,810 --> 00:08:57,262
You love the library.

242
00:08:57,162 --> 00:08:59,387
And coffee at home tastes better.

243
00:08:59,587 --> 00:09:02,564
These new habits don't end on December first.

244
00:09:02,964 --> 00:09:04,508
So you keep three of them.

245
00:09:04,708 --> 00:09:07,319
The wish list. The Sunday food plan.

246
00:09:07,219 --> 00:09:08,644
And no saved cards.

247
00:09:08,844 --> 00:09:11,162
Even half of those savings is over

248
00:09:11,062 --> 00:09:12,989
two thousand dollars a year.

249
00:09:13,189 --> 00:09:15,840
That's the real win of No-Spend November.

250
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:17,345
Want to try it?

251
00:09:17,245 --> 00:09:19,555
Start today. It's November first.

252
00:09:19,755 --> 00:09:21,901
Write your rules. Do the audit.

253
00:09:21,801 --> 00:09:24,343
Close the doors. Start the wish list.

254
00:09:24,543 --> 00:09:26,666
Plan your food. Make a free fun

255
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:28,689
list. Move the money every day.

256
00:09:29,089 --> 00:09:31,720
And remember, these numbers are an example.

257
00:09:31,620 --> 00:09:33,545
Your month will look different.

258
00:09:33,745 --> 00:09:36,370
Maybe you save one hundred dollars.

259
00:09:36,270 --> 00:09:37,669
Maybe six hundred.

260
00:09:37,869 --> 00:09:39,979
Every dollar you keep is a dollar

261
00:09:39,879 --> 00:09:41,137
that works for you.

262
00:09:41,537 --> 00:09:44,041
If this helped, subscribe for one simple

263
00:09:43,941 --> 00:09:45,303
money move every day.

264
00:09:45,503 --> 00:09:47,356
And tell me in the comments...

265
00:09:47,256 --> 00:09:49,693
are you doing No-Spend November with me?

266
00:09:49,893 --> 00:09:51,975
Write 'I'm in,' and I'll check on

267
00:09:51,875 --> 00:09:53,116
you on day fifteen.
